# ── Vercel Deployment / Status ──
# Used by /api/status to fetch LIVE deployment state + commit info from the
# Vercel REST API (readyState, readyAt, githubCommitSha/Ref/Message/Author).
# If unset, the status endpoint falls back to: VERCEL_* build-time Git env vars →
# local `git log` → "UNAVAILABLE". Never expose this token to the client.
# Create: Vercel Dashboard → Settings (vercel.com/account/settings/tokens) → Tokens → Create Token
# Scope: read-only (deployments). Format: `tnt_...` (or legacy hex string).
VERCEL_API_TOKEN=""

# Runtime-deployment attachments (auto-injected by Vercel at build/runtime;
# do NOT hardcode) — listed here for documentation only:
#   VERCEL_DEPLOYMENT_ID
#   VERCEL_ENV                  (production | preview | development)
#   VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA
#   VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_REF
#   VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_MESSAGE
#   VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_AUTHOR_LOGIN
#   VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_AUTHORED_AT
#   VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL

# ── Contact Form (Resend) ──
# Required by /api/send (ContactForm submission → transactional email).
# Create: https://resend.com → API Keys (uses a `re_`-prefixed key).
RESEND_API_KEY=""